cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: AstroRecon
subtitle: >-
  Differentiable General-Relativistic Ray Tracing and Volumetric
  Reconstruction from Astronomical Data
authors:
  - family-names: Chamoli
    given-names: Aaradhya
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: v0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KanhiChamoli/AstroRecon"
keywords:
  - black-hole imaging
  - general relativity
  - ray tracing
  - Event Horizon Telescope
  - Sagittarius A*
  - inverse problems
  - computational astrophysics
  - differentiable programming
abstract: >-
  AstroRecon reconstructs 3D density volumes from 2D astronomical
  observations through a differentiable, GPU-accelerated forward model.
  For compact objects it integrates null geodesics through a Schwarzschild
  spacetime in the Kerr-Schild chart, producing black-hole shadows, photon
  rings, relativistic Doppler beaming, and gravitationally lensed
  starfields from first principles. It supports FITS image/cube
  reconstruction and EHT UVFITS interferometric imaging with
  survey-calibration parameter rows.
